/* Hinglish for Glossary (glossary), in simple words.
   Written by tools/sheet.mjs apply; keyed on the English line. Loads last, so it wins. */
Object.assign(window.HING = window.HING || {}, {
  'Think of a finished homework page that a friend can pick up and check. An artifact is something you made that another person can open and check: a document, a spreadsheet, a notebook, a prototype or a dashboard. In this book, progress is counted in artifacts, not in pages read.':
    'Sochiye ek poora kiya hua homework, jise dost uthakar check kar sake. Artifact woh cheez hai jo aapne banayi aur jise koi doosra khol kar check kar sake: document, spreadsheet, notebook, prototype ya dashboard. Is book mein progress artifacts se gina jaata hai, padhe hue pages se nahi.',
  'Think of the gate at the end of a school year: you pass only if the marks are good enough. The mastery gate is the check at the end of every chapter. Score each artifact 0 to 3, and move on only when all score at least 2 and no safety, privacy or evidence item scores 0.':
    'Sochiye saal ke ant ka gate: achhe marks hon tabhi aap aage jaate hain. Mastery gate har chapter ke ant ka check hai. Har artifact ko 0 se 3 tak score dijiye, aur tabhi aage badhiye jab sab kam se kam 2 hon aur safety, privacy ya evidence ka koi item 0 na ho.',
  'Think of a diary where you write why you chose something, so you can look back later. A decision log is a running file where you record each decision with its date, the evidence behind it, and what would make you change it.':
    'Sochiye ek diary jismein aap likhte hain ki kya aur kyun chuna, taaki baad mein dekh sakein. Decision log ek chalti file hai jismein har decision ki date, uske peeche ka evidence, aur woh baat likhi jaati hai jo aapko decision badalne par majboor karegi.',
  'Think of an online folder that remembers every change you ever made to its files. A repository is a folder on a site such as GitHub that keeps a project\'s files and every earlier version of them, with a note on each change.':
    'Sochiye ek online folder jo apni files mein kiya har badlaav yaad rakhta hai. Repository GitHub jaisi site par ek folder hai jo project ki files aur unke har purane version ko rakhta hai, har badlaav par ek note ke saath.',
  'Think of pressing Save on a document and adding a short note. A commit is one saved version of the files in a repository, with a short message saying what changed.':
    'Sochiye document par Save dabana aur saath mein ek chhota note likhna. Commit repository ki files ka ek saved version hai, ek chhote message ke saath ki kya badla.',
  'Think of a calculator that lives inside one box of a spreadsheet and keeps itself up to date. A formula is a cell in a spreadsheet that starts with = and works out its value from other cells, so it changes when they change.':
    'Sochiye spreadsheet ke ek khaane mein baitha calculator jo khud ko taaza rakhta hai. Formula spreadsheet ka woh cell hai jo = se shuru hota hai aur doosre cells se apni value nikaalta hai, isliye woh badalta hai jab doosre cells badalte hain.',
  'Think of a wholesaler selling to shops, versus a shop selling to you. B2B means business-to-business: you sell to companies, and the people who pay, use and approve the product are often different people. B2C means business-to-consumer: you sell to individuals, who usually pay and use it themselves.':
    'Sochiye thok vyapari jo dukaanon ko bechta hai, aur dukaan jo seedha aapko bechti hai. B2B yaani business-to-business: aap companies ko bechte hain, aur paisa dene wale, use karne wale aur manzoor karne wale aksar alag log hote hain. B2C yaani business-to-consumer: aap individuals ko bechte hain, jo aam taur par khud paisa dete hain aur khud use karte hain.',
  'Think of checking four things before you build a house: will anyone want it, can they live in it, can we build it, and does it pay for itself. Product sense is the habit of checking an idea against four risks before building it: value (will people want it?), usability (can they use it?), feasibility (can we build it?) and viability (does it work for the business?).':
    'Sochiye ghar banane se pehle chaar cheezein dekhna: koi chahega, koi rah paayega, hum bana paayenge, aur kharcha niklega. Product sense yeh aadat hai ki idea banane se pehle use chaar risks par parkho: value (log chahenge?), usability (log use kar paayenge?), feasibility (hum bana paayenge?) aur viability (business ke liye chalega?).',
  'Think of hiring a taxi for one job: to get to the station on time. Jobs to be done is the idea that people "hire" a product to make progress in a particular situation. Write it as: "When [situation], I want to [motivation], so I can [outcome]."':
    'Sochiye ek kaam ke liye taxi kiraye par lena: station time par pahunchna. Jobs to be done ka matlab hai ki log kisi khaas halaat mein aage badhne ke liye product ko "kiraye par lete" hain. Ise aise likhiye: "Jab [halaat], mujhe [chaah] chahiye, taaki main [nateeja] paa sakoon."',
  'Think of a shopkeeper asking, "You liked it, didn\'t you?" A leading question is an interview question that hints at the answer the interviewer wants, such as "Isn\'t it frustrating when...?" People tend to agree, so the answer is weak evidence.':
    'Sochiye dukaandaar poochhe, "Aapko pasand aaya na?" Leading question woh interview sawaal hai jo us jawaab ki taraf ishara karta hai jo poochhne wala sunna chahta hai, jaise "Kya yeh frustrating nahi hai jab...?" Log aksar haan kah dete hain, isliye aisa jawaab kamzor evidence hai.',
  'Think of one made-up character on a poster who stands for a whole group of customers. A persona is a short description of a type of user, their goals, workflow and pains. It is useful only when every line traces back to real interviews.':
    'Sochiye poster par ek kalpanik kirdaar jo customers ke poore group ko dikhata hai. Persona ek tarah ke user ka chhota vivaran hai: unke goals, kaam karne ka tareeka aur dikkatein. Yeh tabhi kaam ka hai jab har line asli interviews se judi ho.',
  'Think of a map of a train trip, with the stations, how the traveller feels at each one, and the bumpy stretches. A journey map shows the steps a user goes through to get a job done, with what they do, think and feel at each step, and where the pain is.':
    'Sochiye train safar ka naqsha: station, har station par yatri ka mood, aur jhatke wale hisse. Journey map woh steps dikhata hai jinse ek user kaam poora karta hai, har step par woh kya karta, sochta aur mehsoos karta hai, aur dikkat kahan hai.',
  'Think of the one beam in a building that you are least sure will hold. The riskiest unknown is the assumption that would do the most damage if it were wrong and that you are least sure of. Test it first.':
    'Sochiye imaarat ki woh ek beam jis par aapko sabse kam bharosa hai. Riskiest unknown woh maani hui baat hai jo galat nikli toh sabse zyaada nuksaan karegi aur jiske baare mein aap sabse kam pakke hain. Ise sabse pehle test kijiye.',
  'Think of three circles inside each other, like a big plate, a smaller plate and a katori. Total addressable market (TAM) is everyone with the problem. Serviceable addressable market (SAM) is the part you can actually serve. Serviceable obtainable market (SOM) is what you could realistically win in a few years.':
    'Sochiye ek ke andar ek, teen gol: badi thaali, chhoti thaali aur katori. Total addressable market (TAM) har woh insaan hai jise yeh problem hai. Serviceable addressable market (SAM) woh hissa hai jise aap asal mein serve kar sakte hain. Serviceable obtainable market (SOM) woh hai jo aap kuchh saalon mein realistically jeet sakte hain.',
  'Think of the one line on a shop board that says who the shop is for and why it is different. A positioning statement is one or two sentences saying who a product is for, what it does for them, and how it differs from the main alternative.':
    'Sochiye dukaan ke board par likhi woh ek line jo batati hai ki dukaan kiske liye hai aur doosron se alag kyun hai. Positioning statement ek ya do vaakya hain jo batate hain ki product kiske liye hai, unke liye kya karta hai, aur mukhya vikalp se alag kaise hai.',
  'Think of the deep water around a fort that enemies cannot easily cross. A moat is an advantage that is hard for competitors to copy, such as deep workflow integration, unique data or earned trust. A prompt or a newer model is not a moat.':
    'Sochiye kile ke chaaron taraf gehra paani jise dushman aasaani se paar nahi kar sakte. Moat woh fayda hai jise competitors ke liye copy karna mushkil ho, jaise kaam ke flow mein gehra judna, anokha data ya kamaya hua bharosa. Ek prompt ya naya model moat nahi hai.',
  'Think of a family tree, but for ideas: one goal at the top, branching down to needs, then ideas, then tests. An opportunity solution tree is a diagram with an outcome at the top, the user needs and pains from interviews below it, then possible solutions, then tests. It stops you jumping straight to a solution.':
    'Sochiye khandaan ka ped, lekin ideas ka: sabse upar ek goal, neeche needs, phir ideas, phir tests. Opportunity solution tree ek diagram hai jismein sabse upar ek outcome hota hai, uske neeche interviews se mile user ki zarooratein aur dikkatein, phir mumkin solutions, phir tests. Yeh aapko seedha solution par kudne se rokta hai.',
  'Think of the thin end of a wedge going into wood: small at the front, and it opens the way for the rest. A wedge is the narrow first use case you can clearly win, chosen because it leads on to something bigger.':
    'Sochiye lakdi mein ghuste hue wedge ka patla sira: aage se chhota, lekin baaki ke liye raasta kholta hai. Wedge woh sankra pehla use case hai jise aap saaf taur par jeet sakte hain, aur jise isliye chuna jaata hai ki woh kisi bade kaam tak le jaata hai.',
  'Think of the Pole Star that sailors steer by: one light to guide the whole crew. The North Star metric is the one number that best measures the value customers get from a product, such as "issues caught in their first week". Chapter B3 covers it in detail.':
    'Sochiye dhruv tara jisse naavik raasta dekhte hain: poore crew ke liye ek roshni. North Star metric woh ek number hai jo sabse achhi tarah naapta hai ki customers ko product se kitni value milti hai, jaise "pehle hafte mein pakde gaye issues". Chapter B3 ise detail mein batata hai.',
  'Think of marking each idea out of its reach, impact and confidence, then dividing by the work. RICE is a prioritisation score: reach × impact × confidence ÷ effort. It helps you compare options in the same way, but it is only as good as the guesses you put in.':
    'Sochiye har idea ko uski pahunch, asar aur bharose se number dena, phir mehnat se bhaag dena. RICE ek prioritisation score hai: reach × impact × confidence ÷ effort. Isse aap options ko ek hi tareeke se taul sakte hain, lekin yeh utna hi achha hai jitne achhe andaaze aap daalte hain.',
  'Think of milk left out of the fridge: every hour you wait, you lose a little more. Cost of delay is what you lose for every week an item waits. It is high when there is a deadline, such as a contract renewal.':
    'Sochiye doodh jo fridge ke bahar chhoda ho: jitni der karenge, utna zyaada nuksaan. Cost of delay woh hai jo aap har hafte kho dete hain jab tak koi kaam ruka rehta hai. Jab deadline ho, jaise contract renewal, tab yeh bahut zyaada hota hai.',
  'Think of a notice board with three columns: now, next and later. An outcome roadmap is a roadmap in these three columns where each item is a result you want, not a feature with a date.':
    'Sochiye teen columns wala notice board: abhi, agla aur baad mein. Outcome roadmap in teen columns mein banaya roadmap hai jahan har item ek nateeja hai jo aap chahte hain, kisi date wali feature nahi.',
  'Think of deciding before a cricket match that you will stop the game if it rains for an hour. A kill criterion is a result, decided in advance, that means you stop working on something. For example: "stop if fewer than half of design partners act on an alert within four weeks".':
    'Sochiye match shuru hone se pehle tay kar lena ki ek ghante baarish hui toh khel rok denge. Kill criterion woh nateeja hai, pehle se tay kiya hua, jiska matlab hai ki ab us kaam par kaam rok do. Jaise: "agar chaar hafte mein aadhe se kam design partners alert par kuchh karte hain, toh ruk jao".',
  'Think of a school goal, "do well in maths", with marks that show you did. OKRs mean objectives and key results. The objective says what you want in words; the 3 to 4 key results are numbers that show you got there. Key results should be outcomes, not outputs.':
    'Sochiye school ka goal, "maths mein achha karna", aur marks jo dikhate hain ki kar liya. OKRs yaani objectives aur key results. Objective shabdon mein batata hai ki aap kya chahte hain; 3 se 4 key results woh number hain jo dikhate hain ki aap wahan pahunche. Key results outcomes hone chahiye, outputs nahi.',
  'Think of the railing on a bridge: it keeps you safe while you race ahead. A guardrail metric is a number that must not get worse while you chase a goal, such as false-alarm rate or cost per customer. It stops a team hitting a target in a way that harms users.':
    'Sochiye pul ki railing: aap tez bhaagte hain, phir bhi woh aapko surakshit rakhti hai. Guardrail metric woh number hai jo goal ke peechhe bhaagte waqt kharab nahi hona chahiye, jaise false-alarm rate ya cost per customer. Yeh team ko aisa target chhoone se rokta hai jisse users ko nuksaan ho.',
  'Think of a seating chart for a wedding: who sits near the stage and who sits at the back. A stakeholder map is a grid of the people involved in a decision, placed by how much influence they have and how much they care. It shows who to work closely with and who can veto.':
    'Sochiye shaadi ka seating chart: kaun stage ke paas baithega aur kaun peechhe. Stakeholder map faisle se jude logon ka grid hai, jinhe is hisaab se rakha jaata hai ki unka kitna asar hai aur unhe kitni parwaah hai. Yeh dikhata hai ki kiske saath nazdeek se kaam karna hai aur kaun veto kar sakta hai.',
  'Think of a doctor writing down, before the operation, how it could go wrong. A pre-mortem means: before starting, imagine the project has failed and write down why. It brings out risks people would not raise about a live plan.':
    'Sochiye operation se pehle doctor ka likhna ki woh kaise bigad sakta hai. Pre-mortem ka matlab hai: shuru karne se pehle maan lijiye ki project fail ho gaya, aur likhiye kyun. Isse woh risks saamne aate hain jo log chalte hue plan ke baare mein nahi uthate.',
  'Think of the recipe card for a dish: what it is, who it is for, how you know it came out right. A PRD (product requirements document) says what to build, for whom and why, starting from the problem and its evidence. Chapter 18 covers the AI-specific version.':
    'Sochiye kisi pakwaan ka recipe card: woh kya hai, kiske liye hai, aur kaise pata chalega ki sahi bana. PRD (product requirements document) batata hai ki kya banana hai, kiske liye aur kyun, problem aur uske evidence se shuru karke. Chapter 18 AI wala version batata hai.',
  'Think of one line on a wish card: what a person wants and why. A user story is one piece of value from the user\'s point of view: "As a [role], I want [action], so that [benefit]." Each story needs acceptance criteria and edge cases.':
    'Sochiye wish card ki ek line: ek insaan kya chahta hai aur kyun. User story user ki nazar se value ka ek tukda hai: "[role] ke roop mein, main [kaam] chahta hoon, taaki [fayda] ho." Har story ko acceptance criteria aur edge cases chahiye.',
  'Think of a street-food cart you open first, before building a restaurant. An MVP (minimum viable product) is the smallest thing that tests your riskiest assumption with real users. It is not a small version of the whole product.':
    'Sochiye khaane ka thela jo aap restaurant banane se pehle kholte hain. MVP (minimum viable product) sabse chhoti cheez hai jo asli users ke saath aapki sabse risky maani hui baat ko test kare. Yeh poore product ka chhota version nahi hai.',
  'Think of cutting a thin slice from a layered cake so you taste every layer at once. A vertical slice is a thin version of a feature that goes through every layer, from input to user value, so a real user can try it early.':
    'Sochiye parat wale cake ka patla tukda kaatna, taaki har parat ek saath chakh sakein. Vertical slice kisi feature ka patla version hai jo har layer se guzarta hai, input se user ki value tak, taaki asli user use jaldi aazma sake.',
  'Think of a kitchen timer set for uncertain cooking. A time-box is a fixed amount of time for uncertain work, with a result that counts as success and a plan if you do not reach it.':
    'Sochiye anishchit pakwaan ke liye lagaya kitchen timer. Time-box anishchit kaam ke liye tay kiya hua samay hai, ek aisa nateeja jo safalta ginega, aur ek plan agar aap wahan nahi pahunche.',
  'Think of watching someone try to open a new tiffin box without helping. A usability test means watching a real user try to complete a task with your product, without helping, to see where they get stuck.':
    'Sochiye kisi ko naya tiffin box kholte hue dekhna, bina madad kiye. Usability test ka matlab hai ek asli user ko aapke product se kaam poora karte dekhna, bina madad kiye, taaki dikhe ki woh kahan atakta hai.',
  'Think of a reader who looks at the whole page at once and picks out which earlier words matter most. A transformer is the model design behind today\'s LLMs. It reads every token in the context at once and learns which earlier tokens matter for predicting the next one.':
    'Sochiye ek paathak jo poora page ek saath dekhta hai aur chunta hai ki pehle ke kaun se shabd sabse zaroori hain. Transformer aaj ke LLMs ke peechhe ka model design hai. Yeh context ka har token ek saath padhta hai aur seekhta hai ki agla token guess karne ke liye pehle ke kaun se tokens zaroori hain.',
  'Think of a student sitting the exam, not studying for it. Inference means running a trained model to get an answer. Training changes the model; inference only uses it. Most of your bill is inference.':
    'Sochiye woh student jo exam de raha hai, padh nahi raha. Inference ka matlab hai trained model chalakar jawaab lena. Training model ko badalti hai; inference sirf use karti hai. Aapke bill ka zyaadatar hissa inference ka hota hai.',
  'Think of a child reading a whole library before ever going to school. Pre-training is the first and most expensive training stage: the model learns to predict the next token over a huge amount of text.':
    'Sochiye ek bachcha jo school jaane se pehle poori library padh leta hai. Pre-training pehla aur sabse mehenga training stage hai: model bahut saare text par agla token guess karna seekhta hai.',
  'Think of the parrot going to a small class where it learns to answer questions, not just keep talking. Instruction tuning is training after pre-training on examples of instructions and good answers, so the model follows requests instead of just continuing text.':
    'Sochiye tota jo ek chhoti class mein jaata hai jahan woh sawaalon ka jawaab dena seekhta hai, bas bolte rehna nahi. Instruction tuning pre-training ke baad ki training hai, jismein instructions aur achhe jawaabon ke examples hote hain, taaki model request maane, sirf text aage na badhaye.',
  'Think of a teacher marking which of two answers is better, and the student learning from the marks. RLHF means reinforcement learning from human feedback. People rank model answers, and the model is trained toward the answers they prefer.':
    'Sochiye teacher jo do jawaabon mein se behtar par nishaan lagata hai, aur student un nishaanon se seekhta hai. RLHF yaani reinforcement learning from human feedback. Log model ke jawaabon ko rank karte hain, aur model ko unke pasand ke jawaabon ki taraf train kiya jaata hai.',
  'Think of a recipe book you can take home and cook from in your own kitchen, instead of ordering from a restaurant. An open-weight model is one whose trained weights are published, so you can download and run it yourself instead of calling a vendor\'s API.':
    'Sochiye recipe ki kitaab jo aap ghar le jaakar apni rasoi mein bana sakte hain, restaurant se mangwane ke bajaye. Open-weight model woh hai jiske trained weights chhape hue hain, taaki aap use khud download karke chala sakein, vendor ki API ko call karne ke bajaye.',
  'Think of the most you would pay a plumber when your pipe has burst, set by how bad the leak is, not by what the plumber spends. Willingness to pay is the most a buyer would spend to solve a problem. It is set by what their current alternative costs them, not by your costs.':
    'Sochiye woh sabse zyaada rakam jo aap plumber ko denge jab paip phat jaye, jo leak kitni buri hai us par tikti hai, plumber ke kharche par nahi. Willingness to pay woh sabse zyaada hai jo khareedar kisi problem ko hal karne ke liye dega. Yeh is par tikta hai ki unka abhi ka vikalp unhe kitna padta hai, aapke kharche par nahi.',
  'Think of a tea stall: what is left from each customer after you pay for the milk, sugar and helper that grow with each cup. Contribution margin is what each customer leaves you after the costs that grow with them, such as model calls and support. It is usually shown as a percentage of revenue.':
    'Sochiye chai ki tapri: har customer se jo bachta hai doodh, cheeni aur madadgaar ka kharcha dene ke baad, jo har cup ke saath badhta hai. Contribution margin woh hai jo har customer aapke paas chhodta hai un kharchon ke baad jo unke saath badhte hain, jaise model calls aur support. Ise aam taur par revenue ke percentage mein dikhaya jaata hai.',
  'Think of a shop\'s sale minus what the goods cost it. Gross margin is revenue minus the direct cost of delivering the product. For AI products, the model vendor\'s bill is a large part of that cost.':
    'Sochiye dukaan ki bikri minus maal ki laagat. Gross margin revenue minus product dene ki seedhi laagat hai. AI products mein model vendor ka bill us laagat ka bada hissa hota hai.',
  'Think of a heavy wheel: once it spins, each push makes the next one easier. A flywheel is a loop where using the product makes it better, which brings more use. It can run on data, on workflow habits or on others building on you.':
    'Sochiye ek bhaari chakka: ek baar ghoom jaye toh har dhakka agle ko aasaan bana deta hai. Flywheel ek loop hai jahan product use karne se woh behtar hota hai, jisse aur use hota hai. Yeh data par, kaam ki aadaton par ya doosron ke aap par banane par chal sakta hai.',
  'Think of paying the tailor per finished shirt, not per hour. Outcome pricing means charging for each successful result, such as a resolved ticket, rather than for seats or usage. It needs an agreed way to measure success.':
    'Sochiye darzi ko har tayyar shirt ke hisaab se paisa dena, ghante ke hisaab se nahi. Outcome pricing ka matlab hai har safal nateeje ka paisa lena, jaise ek hal hua ticket, seats ya use ke bajaye. Iske liye safalta naapne ka ek tay tareeka chahiye.',
  'Think of a path with five stops: people hear of you, try you, stay, tell friends and pay. AARRR is five stages of growth: acquisition, activation, retention, referral and revenue. Each stage gets one event you can count.':
    'Sochiye paanch padaav wala raasta: log aapko jaante hain, aazmate hain, rukte hain, doston ko batate hain aur paisa dete hain. AARRR growth ke paanch stages hain: acquisition, activation, retention, referral aur revenue. Har stage ke liye ek event hota hai jise aap gin sakte hain.',
  'Think of the first sip of good chai, when the customer says, "Ah, this is it." The activation moment is the first time a new user gets the value your product promises.':
    'Sochiye achhi chai ka pehla ghoont, jab customer kahe, "Haan, yahi chahiye tha." Activation moment woh pehli baar hai jab naya user woh value paata hai jiska aapka product vaada karta hai.',
  'Think of how long you wait from placing your chai order to the first sip. Time-to-value is how long a new user takes to reach the activation moment, measured from sign-up.':
    'Sochiye chai ka order dene se pehle ghoont tak kitni der lagti hai. Time-to-value woh samay hai jo naya user activation moment tak pahunchne mein leta hai, sign-up se naapa hua.',
  'Think of a chain of dominoes: each fall knocks over the next. A growth loop is a cycle where one user\'s actions bring in the next user, so the output feeds back into the input.':
    'Sochiye dominoes ki kadi: har gira domino agle ko giraata hai. Growth loop ek chakra hai jahan ek user ke kaam agle user ko laate hain, isliye output wapas input mein jaata hai.',
  'Think of a phone: it is useless alone, and better with every friend who owns one. A network effect is when a product gets better for existing users as more people use it. It is different from virality, which only brings more people in.':
    'Sochiye phone: akela bekaar, aur har dost ke paas hone se behtar. Network effect tab hota hai jab product mojooda users ke liye behtar hota hai jaise zyaada log use karte hain. Yeh virality se alag hai, jo sirf aur logon ko laati hai.',
  'Think of a rumour spreading through a mohalla: more people hear it, but the rumour itself does not get better. Virality is users bringing in other users, for example by sharing. It helps growth, but does not make the product better for anyone.':
    'Sochiye mohalle mein failti afwah: zyaada log sunte hain, lekin afwah khud behtar nahi hoti. Virality tab hai jab users doosre users ko laate hain, jaise share karke. Yeh growth mein madad karti hai, lekin kisi ke liye product behtar nahi banati.',
  'Think of a shop with a hidden exit door and a pre-ticked box saying "yes, send me offers". A dark pattern is a design that tricks users into acting against their own interest, such as a hidden cancel button or pre-ticked invitations.':
    'Sochiye dukaan jahan nikalne ka darwaaza chhupa ho aur "haan, mujhe offers bhejo" ka dabba pehle se tick ho. Dark pattern aisa design hai jo users ko apne hi khilaaf kaam karne par phusla deta hai, jaise chhupa hua cancel button ya pehle se tick kiye invitations.',
  'Think of a free sample stall in a market: you taste, you like it, and you buy without a salesman. Product-led growth is a go-to-market motion where users sign up and get value on their own, and some upgrade to paid, without talking to sales.':
    'Sochiye bazaar mein free sample ka stall: aap chakhte hain, pasand aata hai, aur bina salesman ke khareedte hain. Product-led growth ek go-to-market tareeka hai jahan users khud sign up karke value paate hain, aur kuchh paid mein badalte hain, bina sales se baat kiye.',
  'Think of the pedals on a bicycle: you push them directly, and the bike speeds up. An input metric is a number the team can move directly, which you expect to move the North Star metric.':
    'Sochiye cycle ke pedal: aap unhe seedha dabate hain, aur cycle tez hoti hai. Input metric woh number hai jise team seedha hila sakti hai, aur jisse aap umeed karte hain ki North Star metric hilega.',
  'Think of a labelled register where every event gets one name in one fixed style. An event taxonomy is the list of events a product logs, with a naming rule everyone follows, such as object_action.':
    'Sochiye label wala register jahan har event ko ek tay style mein ek naam milta hai. Event taxonomy un events ki list hai jo product log karta hai, ek naam rakhne ke niyam ke saath jo sab maante hain, jaise object_action.',
  'Think of a shared checklist pinned to the wall of the office. A tracking plan is the shared document listing every event, its properties, when it fires and who owns it.':
    'Sochiye office ki deewar par lagi saajhi checklist. Tracking plan woh saajha document hai jismein har event, uski properties, woh kab chalta hai aur uska maalik kaun hai, likha hota hai.',
  'Think of a funnel for pouring oil: wide at the top, narrow at the bottom. A funnel is the share of users who complete each step of a process in order. It shows where people drop off.':
    'Sochiye tel daalne ki funnel: upar chauri, neeche sankri. Funnel un users ka hissa hai jo kisi process ka har step kram mein poora karte hain. Yeh dikhata hai ki log kahan chhodte hain.',
  'Think of a school batch: everyone who joined in the same year. A cohort is a group of users who started in the same period. Retention tables follow each cohort over time.':
    'Sochiye school ka batch: sab jo ek hi saal mein aaye. Cohort un users ka group hai jinhone ek hi samay mein shuru kiya. Retention tables har cohort ko samay ke saath follow karte hain.',
  'Think of a weighing scale that cannot show less than 10 grams: below that, you cannot tell. Minimum detectable effect is the smallest change an experiment is designed to detect. It sets how many users the test needs.':
    'Sochiye tarazu jo 10 gram se kam nahi dikha sakta: usse neeche aap farq nahi bata sakte. Minimum detectable effect sabse chhota badlaav hai jo ek experiment pakadne ke liye banaya gaya hai. Isi se tay hota hai ki test ko kitne users chahiye.',
  'Think of asking only the front-row students how the class went. Selection bias is when the people in your data differ from the people you want to learn about, such as hand-picked early users.':
    'Sochiye class kaisi rahi, yeh sirf aage ki line ke students se poochhna. Selection bias tab hota hai jab aapke data ke log un logon se alag hon jinke baare mein aap jaanna chahte hain, jaise chun-chun kar liye gaye shuruaati users.',
  'Think of a snakes-and-ladders board: every square and every move is fixed in advance. A state machine is a workflow where code fixes every step and every transition. The failing step is always known.':
    'Sochiye saanp-seedhi ka board: har khaana aur har chaal pehle se tay. State machine ek workflow hai jahan code har step aur har badlaav tay karta hai. Jo step fail hota hai woh hamesha pata hota hai.',
  'Think of a helper with a list of errands, a fixed set of tools and a curfew. A bounded agent is an agent that chooses its own steps, but only from a fixed tool list and within a step budget and approval rules.':
    'Sochiye ek madadgaar jiske paas errands ki list, tay auzaar aur ghar lautne ka waqt hai. Bounded agent woh agent hai jo apne steps khud chunta hai, lekin sirf ek tay tool list se aur step budget aur approval rules ke andar.',
  'Think of the ticket checker at the railway gate: nobody gets through without the right ticket. A release gate is a check that must pass before a change reaches users. For AI products it includes eval thresholds as well as tests.':
    'Sochiye railway gate ka ticket checker: sahi ticket ke bina koi andar nahi jaata. Release gate woh check hai jo users tak badlaav pahunchne se pehle paas hona chahiye. AI products mein ismein tests ke saath eval thresholds bhi aate hain.',
  'Think of a neighbour who agrees to taste your half-cooked dish and tell you what is wrong. A design partner is an early user who agrees to use an unfinished product and tell you what they find, with clear consent.':
    'Sochiye padosi jo aapka aadha pakka khaana chakhne aur kya kami hai bataane ko raazi ho. Design partner ek shuruaati user hai jo adhoore product ko use karne aur jo mile woh batane ko raazi hota hai, saaf sahmati ke saath.',
  'Think of a notice at the shop door saying what changed this week. A changelog is a short public note of what changed in each release, why, and what users should do differently.':
    'Sochiye dukaan ke darwaaze par lagi suchna ki is hafte kya badla. Changelog har release mein kya badla, kyun, aur users ko kya alag karna chahiye, uska chhota saarvajanik note hai.',
  'Think of a table with job ads down the side and skills across the top, ticked where a job asks for a skill. A role matrix is a grid of real job descriptions against the skills they ask for, used to find the skills the market wants and your gaps.':
    'Sochiye ek table jismein side mein job ads aur upar skills hain, jahan job kisi skill ko maangti hai wahan tick. Role matrix asli job descriptions ka grid hai jo unki maangi skills ke saamne rakha jaata hai, taaki pata chale ki market kaun si skills chahta hai aur aapki kami kahan hai.',
  'A model (an LLM) is like a parrot that has read a whole library. It is a prediction machine trained on huge amounts of text. It continues a piece of text in a way that sounds likely, and it does not look things up.':
    'Model (LLM) ek aise tote jaisa hai jisne poori library padh li ho. Yeh ek prediction machine hai jise bahut saare text par train kiya gaya hai. Yeh text ko aise aage badhata hai jo sunne mein sahi lage, aur kuchh look up nahi karta.',
  'Think of an SMS that costs a few paise: one message goes in, one reply comes out, and you pay once. An API call is your app sending a request to the model\'s servers and waiting for the reply.':
    'Sochiye ek SMS jisme kuchh paise lagte hain: ek message jaata hai, ek reply aata hai, aur aap ek baar paisa dete hain. API call mein aapka app model ke servers ko request bhejta hai aur reply ka intezaar karta hai.',
  'Think of one Lego brick of text. A token is a small piece of a word, and it is the unit a model reads, writes and bills in. One token is roughly ¾ of an English word.':
    'Sochiye text ki ek Lego eent. Token word ka ek chhota tukda hai, aur model isi unit mein padhta, likhta aur bill banata hai. Ek token lagbhag ek English word ka ¾ hota hai.',
  'Think of the model\'s desk: only what fits on it can be read at once. The context window is the most text a model can handle in one request, counting everything that goes in and everything that comes out, together.':
    'Sochiye model ki mez: jo mez par fit ho wahi ek baar mein padha ja sakta hai. Context window woh sabse zyaada text hai jo model ek request mein sambhal sakta hai, jismein jo andar jaata hai aur jo bahar aata hai, dono ek saath ginte jaate hain.',
  'Think of a goldfish: it forgets everything after each message, unless you send the old chat again. Stateless means the model remembers nothing between requests. Each request starts from a blank slate on the model\'s side.':
    'Sochiye goldfish: har message ke baad sab bhool jaati hai, jab tak aap purani chat dobara na bhejein. Stateless ka matlab hai ki model requests ke beech kuchh yaad nahi rakhta. Model ki taraf se har request saaf slate se shuru hoti hai.',
  'Think of the bill that comes with each reply. The usage block is the receipt for a request. It shows how many prompt tokens were read in and how many completion tokens were written out.':
    'Sochiye har reply ke saath aane wala bill. Usage block ek request ki receipt hai. Isme dikhta hai ki kitne prompt tokens andar padhe gaye aur kitne completion tokens bahar likhe gaye.',
  'Think of the standing rules on the shop wall, read before every order. A system prompt is a standing instruction that goes along with every message, out of the user\'s sight. It tells the AI how to behave.':
    'Sochiye dukaan ki deewar par lage niyam, jo har order se pehle padhe jaate hain. System prompt ek tay nirdesh hai jo har message ke saath jaata hai, user ki nazar se door. Yeh AI ko batata hai ki kaise pesh aana hai.',
  'Think of how adventurous the model is with its next word. Temperature is a setting that decides whether the AI always picks its most likely next guess (plays safe) or sometimes picks a less likely one (takes chances). A low setting gives repeatable answers. It does not make them true.':
    'Sochiye model apne agle word mein kitna jokhim leta hai. Temperature ek setting hai jo tay karti hai ki AI hamesha apna sabse mumkin agla guess chune (safe khele) ya kabhi kam mumkin wala chune (jokhim le). Kam setting se baar-baar ek jaise jawaab milte hain. Isse woh sach nahi ho jaate.',
  'Think of confident make-believe: a made-up answer said with a straight face. A hallucination is when the AI gives you something that sounds fluent but is made up, because it had no evidence to go on. This is not a malfunction. It is how a guessing machine normally behaves when it has nothing to go on.':
    'Sochiye pakke yakeen se boli gayi banawati baat: ek gadha hua jawaab seedhe chehre ke saath. Hallucination tab hota hai jab AI aisi cheez deta hai jo saaf-suthri sunayi deti hai lekin banawati hai, kyunki uske paas koi evidence nahi tha. Yeh kharabi nahi hai. Jab guess karne wali machine ke paas kuchh nahi hota, woh aam taur par aise hi karti hai.',
  'Think of the railing on a bridge: it stops a fall, it does not drive the car. A guardrail is anything that reduces harmful or wrong outputs. The simplest kind is a single sentence in the system prompt.':
    'Sochiye pul ki railing: yeh girne se rokti hai, gaadi nahi chalati. Guardrail woh har cheez hai jo nuksaandeh ya galat outputs ko kam kare. Sabse saral prakar system prompt mein ek vaakya hai.',
  'Think of one index card cut from a long book. A chunk is one piece of a document after it has been cut up. It is the unit that gets stored, searched and sent to the model.':
    'Sochiye lambi kitaab se kaata gaya ek index card. Chunk ek document ka woh tukda hai jo kaatne ke baad bana. Yahi woh unit hai jo store hota hai, search hota hai aur model ko bheja jaata hai.',
  'Think of cutting a long book into index cards. Chunking is the cutting itself. It looks like a boring chore, but it is a real design decision.':
    'Sochiye lambi kitaab ko index cards mein kaatna. Chunking khud yeh kaatne ka kaam hai. Yeh ek ubaau kaam lagta hai, lekin yeh ek asli design decision hai.',
  'Think of cutting a roll of cloth every metre, whatever the pattern. Fixed-size chunking is cutting after every N words, whatever the text means.':
    'Sochiye kapde ke thaan ko har meter par kaatna, design chahe kuchh bhi ho. Fixed-size chunking har N words ke baad kaatna hai, text ka matlab chahe kuchh bhi ho.',
  'Think of cutting a book at its chapter ends, not in the middle of a page. Semantic chunking is cutting at the places where the document\'s own structure divides it.':
    'Sochiye kitaab ko uske chapter ke ant par kaatna, page ke beech mein nahi. Semantic chunking wahan kaatna hai jahan document ka apna dhancha use baantta hai.',
  'Think of the last line of one page being printed again at the top of the next. Chunk overlap is repeating the last lines of one chunk at the start of the next one. That way, an answer that sits across the boundary is not lost.':
    'Sochiye ek page ki aakhri line ka agle page ke upar dobara chhapna. Chunk overlap ek chunk ki aakhri lines ko agle chunk ke shuru mein dohrana hai. Isse jo jawaab do chunks ki seema par ho, woh kho nahi jaata.',
  'Think of an open-book exam: first find the right page. Retrieval is fetching, from all the stored chunks, the few that are most likely to answer a question.':
    'Sochiye open-book exam: pehle sahi page dhoondhiye. Retrieval sabhi stored chunks mein se woh thode chunks laana hai jo sawaal ka jawaab dene ke sabse kareeb hon.',
  'Think of Ctrl+F: it finds the exact word you typed. Keyword search finds text by the words it shares with the question. It matches spelling and is blind to meaning.':
    'Sochiye Ctrl+F: yeh aapka likha hua ekdum wahi word dhoondhta hai. Keyword search text ko un words se dhoondhta hai jo sawaal ke saath milte hain. Yeh spelling milata hai aur matlab ke liye andha hai.',
  'Think of the slip you hand the librarian with your question on it. The query is the question that comes in.':
    'Sochiye woh parchi jo aap librarian ko dete hain jis par aapka sawaal likha hai. Query woh sawaal hai jo andar aata hai.',
  'Think of asking two helpers, one who matches exact words and one who matches meaning, and then combining their lists. Hybrid search runs keyword search and semantic search together, then merges their results.':
    'Sochiye do madadgaaron se poochhna, ek jo ekdum wahi words milata hai aur ek jo matlab milata hai, phir dono ki list milana. Hybrid search keyword search aur semantic search ko saath chalata hai, phir unke results milata hai.',
  'Think of picking only the top k students from a merit list. Top-k means take only the best k results. The number k is a dial between recall (not missing anything) and precision (not carrying junk).':
    'Sochiye merit list se sirf upar ke k students chunna. Top-k ka matlab hai sirf sabse achhe k results lena. Number k ek ghumaane wala dial hai recall (kuchh na chhootna) aur precision (kachra na uthana) ke beech.',
  'Think of an address for meaning: sentences that mean the same thing live on the same street. An embedding is the position a piece of text gets on the meaning map, written as a list of numbers. A small AI whose only job is placing text produces it.':
    'Sochiye matlab ka pata: jin vaakyon ka matlab ek jaisa hai, woh ek hi gali mein rehte hain. Embedding woh jagah hai jo text ko matlab ke naqshe par milti hai, numbers ki list ke roop mein likhi hui. Ise ek chhota AI banata hai jiska ek hi kaam text ko jagah dena hai.',
  'Think of the mapmaker who gives every sentence its address. An embedding model reads text and gives back its address on the meaning map.':
    'Sochiye naqshanavis jo har vaakya ko uska pata deta hai. Embedding model text padhta hai aur matlab ke naqshe par uska pata wapas deta hai.',
  'Think of measuring how close two houses are on the meaning map. Cosine similarity is a quick test of how close two pieces of text are. The higher the number, the closer they are in meaning.':
    'Sochiye matlab ke naqshe par do gharon ki doori naapna. Cosine similarity do text tukdon ke kareeb hone ki jaldi jaanch hai. Number jitna zyaada, matlab mein woh utne kareeb.',
  'Think of finding a house by its address on the meaning map, not by what its name looks like. Semantic search finds text by its address on the meaning map, instead of by its spelling.':
    'Sochiye kisi ghar ko matlab ke naqshe par uske pate se dhoondhna, naam kaisa dikhta hai us se nahi. Semantic search text ko matlab ke naqshe par uske pate se dhoondhta hai, spelling se nahi.',
  'Think of a sticker on a letter saying "question" or "page from a book". Query vs. passage is a label you give when you create an embedding, saying whether the text is a question or a piece of a document. If you skip it, quality drops quietly and nothing warns you.':
    'Sochiye chitthi par chipka sticker jis par "sawaal" ya "kitaab ka page" likha ho. Query vs. passage ek label hai jo aap embedding banate waqt dete hain, jo batata hai ki text sawaal hai ya document ka tukda. Agar aap ise chhod dein, toh quality chupchaap girti hai aur koi chetavani nahi aati.',
  'Think of a huge cupboard of address cards that can quickly find the ones nearest to yours. A vector database is a system that stores embeddings and can quickly find the ones nearest to a given one.':
    'Sochiye pate ke cards ki bahut badi almari jo tezi se aapke card ke sabse paas wale dhoondh leti hai. Vector database ek system hai jo embeddings store karta hai aur kisi diye hue ke sabse paas wale tezi se dhoondh sakta hai.',
  'Think of the teacher marking your paper against an answer key. Evaluation is grading your system against answers you have already checked. It is like acceptance testing, but for AI.':
    'Sochiye teacher jo aapki copy ko answer key se milakar number deta hai. Evaluation aapke system ko un jawaabon se milakar parakhna hai jo aap pehle se check kar chuke hain. Yeh acceptance testing jaisa hai, lekin AI ke liye.',
  'Think of the teacher\'s answer key: questions with right answers, written before the test. Ground truth is a set of questions with verified correct answers, written before you test anything. Without one, "is it good?" has no answer.':
    'Sochiye teacher ki answer key: sahi jawaabon wale sawaal, test se pehle likhe hue. Ground truth sawaalon ka ek set hai jinke sahi jawaab jaanche hue hain, aur jo aapke kuchh bhi test karne se pehle likhe jaate hain. Iske bina "kya yeh achha hai?" ka koi jawaab nahi.',
  'Think of a net in a pond: of all the fish in the pond, how many did your net catch? Recall is, out of everything that mattered, how much you fetched. Low recall means you missed files.':
    'Sochiye talaab mein jaal: talaab ki saari machhliyon mein se aapke jaal ne kitni pakdi? Recall hai ki jo kuchh mayne rakhta tha, usmein se aapne kitna laaya. Kam recall ka matlab hai ki aapse files chhoot gayin.',
  'Think of the net again: of what is in your net, how much is really fish? Precision is, out of everything you fetched, how much mattered. Low precision means a desk buried in paper.':
    'Phir jaal sochiye: jo aapke jaal mein hai, usmein kitna asal machhli hai? Precision hai ki jo aap laaye, usmein se kitna mayne rakhta tha. Kam precision ka matlab hai kaagzon mein dabi mez.',
  'Think of the pass marks you and the teacher agree on before the exam. Acceptance criteria are the numbers and behaviours you agree on in advance, which the system must meet before it goes live.':
    'Sochiye pass hone ke woh marks jo aap aur teacher exam se pehle tay karte hain. Acceptance criteria woh numbers aur vyavhaar hain jo aap pehle se tay karte hain, jinhe system ko live hone se pehle poora karna hota hai.',
  'Think of an open-book exam: first find the right page, then answer from it. RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) means you first retrieve text that has been checked, then the model writes its answer from that text.':
    'Sochiye open-book exam: pehle sahi page dhoondho, phir usi se jawaab do. RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) ka matlab hai ki aap pehle jaanche hue text ko retrieve karte hain, phir model usi text se apna jawaab likhta hai.',
  'Think of a form with fixed boxes. A schema is a formal description of the shape an output must have: which fields it has, their types, and which are required.':
    'Sochiye fixed khaanon wala form. Schema us aakar ka ek pakka vivaran hai jo output ka hona chahiye: usmein kaun se fields hain, unke types kya hain, aur kaun se zaroori hain.',
  'Think of a model filling in a form instead of writing a letter. Structured output is model output that is held to a schema, instead of free-flowing prose.':
    'Sochiye model chitthi likhne ke bajaye form bhar raha hai. Structured output woh model output hai jo schema ke andar bandha ho, khuli-khuli likhai ke bajaye.',
  'Think of a keyboard that only lets you press the keys that fit the form. Constrained decoding means that at each step the model is allowed to pick only tokens that fit the schema. That makes invalid output impossible, not just unlikely.':
    'Sochiye keyboard jo sirf wahi keys dabane deta hai jo form mein fit hon. Constrained decoding mein har step par model ko sirf woh tokens chunne diye jaate hain jo schema mein fit hon. Isse galat output sirf kam sambhav nahi hota, namumkin ho jaata hai.',
  'Think of a dropdown menu: you can only pick from the list. An enum is a field that can only hold a value from a fixed list.':
    'Sochiye dropdown menu: aap sirf list mein se hi chun sakte hain. Enum ek field hai jo sirf ek tay list mein se hi value rakh sakta hai.',
  'Think of a clerk who says "I cannot tell" instead of making something up. A refusal path is what the product does when it should not answer. It gives a structured way to say "cannot determine" instead of inventing something. You design it on purpose, or it happens by accident.':
    'Sochiye woh clerk jo kuchh gadhne ke bajaye kehta hai "main bata nahi sakta". Refusal path woh hai jo product tab karta hai jab use jawaab nahi dena chahiye. Yeh "tay nahi kar sakte" kehne ka ek structured tareeka deta hai, kuchh gadhne ke bajaye. Ise aap jaan-boojhkar banate hain, warna yeh ittefaq se hota hai.',
  'Think of a teacher who hands a wrong form back with the mistake circled. A validation loop means: parse the output, validate it, and if it fails, ask again with the error attached.':
    'Sochiye teacher jo galat form wapas deta hai, galti par gola lagakar. Validation loop ka matlab hai: output ko parse karo, validate karo, aur agar fail ho toh error saath lagakar dobara poochho.',
  'Think of the model asking a shopkeeper to check the stock for it. Tool calling (function calling) means you describe functions that can be called, so the model can ask for one to be run instead of answering in prose.':
    'Sochiye model dukaandaar se kehta hai ki zara stock check kar do. Tool calling (function calling) mein aap un functions ka vivaran dete hain jo call ho sakte hain, taaki model unmein se ek chalwane ko keh sake, likhe hue jawaab ke bajaye.',
  'Think of a helper going back and forth on errands: ask, do, report, repeat. An agent loop is when the model asks for a tool, your code runs it, the result goes back to the model, and this repeats.':
    'Sochiye madadgaar jo errands par baar-baar jaata hai: poochho, karo, batao, dohrao. Agent loop tab hai jab model ek tool maangta hai, aapka code use chalata hai, nateeja model ko wapas jaata hai, aur yeh dohraya jaata hai.',
  'Think of a curfew for the helper: be home by ten. A step budget is a hard limit on how many times the loop may run. It is not optional.':
    'Sochiye madadgaar ka curfew: dus baje tak ghar aa jao. Step budget is baat ki kadi seema hai ki loop kitni baar chal sakta hai. Yeh vaikalpik nahi hai.',
  'Think of the route the helper took, not just where he ended up. A trace is the recorded list of steps, calls, arguments and results for one run.':
    'Sochiye madadgaar ka liya hua raasta, sirf yeh nahi ki woh kahan pahuncha. Trace ek run ke steps, calls, arguments aur results ki record ki hui list hai.',
  'Think of the difference between looking at a shop window and moving the goods. A side-effect boundary is the line between tools that only read and tools that change something in the world.':
    'Sochiye dukaan ki khidki se dekhne aur maal hilane mein farq. Side-effect boundary woh rekha hai jo sirf padhne wale tools ko un tools se alag karti hai jo duniya mein kuchh badal dete hain.',
  'Think of packing the model\'s desk: what goes on it, in what order, and what gets pushed off. Context engineering is deciding what goes into the context window (the envelope), in what order, and what gets pushed out. It is about the contents, not about how the prompt is worded.':
    'Sochiye model ki mez sajana: kya rakhna hai, kis kram mein, aur kya hata dena hai. Context engineering tay karna hai ki context window (lifaafe) mein kya jaaye, kis kram mein, aur kya bahar dhakela jaaye. Yeh andar ke samaan ke baare mein hai, is baare mein nahi ki prompt kaise likha gaya.',
  'Think of a desk so cluttered that you start missing things you can see. Context rot is when the model uses its context less well as the context grows, long before it hits the limit.':
    'Sochiye itni bhari mez ki jo cheezein saamne hain woh bhi chhootne lagti hain. Context rot tab hota hai jab context badhne par model use kam achhe se istemal karta hai, limit tak pahunchne se bahut pehle.',
  'Think of remembering the start and the end of a long film but not the middle. Lost in the middle means the model finds material at the start and the end far more reliably than material in the middle.':
    'Sochiye lambi film ka shuru aur ant yaad rehna lekin beech ka nahi. Lost in the middle ka matlab hai ki model shuru aur ant ki cheezein beech ki cheezon se kahin zyaada bharosemand tareeke se dhoondhta hai.',
  'Think of a shopkeeper who already knows your usual order, so he starts at once. Prompt caching means the provider reuses the part at the start of a request that it has already processed. Put the stable parts first and the changing parts last.':
    'Sochiye dukaandaar jo aapka roz ka order jaanta hai aur seedha shuru kar deta hai. Prompt caching ka matlab hai ki provider request ke shuru ka woh hissa dobara kaam mein leta hai jo woh pehle hi process kar chuka hai. Na badalne wale hisse pehle rakhiye aur badalne wale baad mein.',
  'Think of squeezing the old pages of a notebook into a short summary so there is room to write, while keeping the latest page as it is. Compaction is summarising older context to free up budget, while keeping the most recent part word for word.':
    'Sochiye copy ke purane pages ko chhote saar mein sametna taaki likhne ki jagah bane, aur sabse naya page jaisa hai waisa rakhna. Compaction purane context ka saar banakar budget khaali karna hai, jabki sabse naya hissa shabd-ba-shabd rakha jaata hai.',
  'Think of a student who does rough work on paper before writing the final answer. A reasoning model does some working-out of its own before it gives its answer. It is slower, and sometimes better.':
    'Sochiye student jo final jawaab likhne se pehle kachche kaagaz par hisaab karta hai. Reasoning model jawaab dene se pehle apna kuchh hisaab khud karta hai. Yeh dheema hai, aur kabhi-kabhi behtar.',
  'Think of giving the student more time on each question during the exam, instead of more years of school. Test-time compute means paying for more accuracy on each query while the model runs, instead of paying for it during training.':
    'Sochiye exam ke dauraan student ko har sawaal par zyaada samay dena, school ke zyaada saal dene ke bajaye. Test-time compute ka matlab hai ki model chalte waqt har query par zyaada sahi jawaab ke liye paisa dena, training ke dauraan dene ke bajaye.',
  'Think of how many sheets of rough paper the student is allowed. The thinking budget is the setting that controls how much working-out the model is allowed. Setting it is a product decision.':
    'Sochiye student ko kachche kaagaz ke kitne panne milte hain. Thinking budget woh setting hai jo tay karti hai ki model ko kitna hisaab karne ki ijaazat hai. Ise tay karna ek product decision hai.',
  'Think of waiting for chai: the middle customer\'s wait, and the wait of the unlucky few at the back. p50 latency is the median response time; p95 latency is the response time of the slow tail. Users feel the tail.':
    'Sochiye chai ka intezaar: beech wale customer ka intezaar, aur peechhe ke kuchh bad-kismat logon ka intezaar. p50 latency madhyak response time hai; p95 latency dheemi poonchh ka response time hai. Users poonchh ko mehsoos karte hain.',
  'Think of Ctrl+F that counts rare words as worth more than common ones. BM25 is a statistical way of ranking keyword matches that gives more weight to rare words. It is Chapter 4\'s scoreboard, done properly.':
    'Sochiye Ctrl+F jo durlabh words ko aam words se zyaada keemti maanta hai. BM25 keyword matches ko rank karne ka ek aankdon wala tareeka hai jo durlabh words ko zyaada vazan deta hai. Yeh Chapter 4 ka scoreboard hai, theek se banaya hua.',
  'Think of two judges each giving a ranked list, and you add up how well each item did. Reciprocal rank fusion merges ranked lists by adding up 1/(rank) for each item. It is simple, sturdy and hard to beat.':
    'Sochiye do judge jo apni-apni rank list dete hain, aur aap dekhte hain ki har item ne kitna achha kiya. Reciprocal rank fusion ranked lists ko milata hai, har item ke liye 1/(rank) jodkar. Yeh saral hai, mazboot hai aur ise harana mushkil hai.',
  'Think of a second teacher who reads the question and each answer card together before giving marks. A reranker is a model that scores a (question, chunk) pair by reading both together. You apply it only to a short list.':
    'Sochiye doosre teacher jo number dene se pehle sawaal aur har answer card ko saath padhte hain. Reranker ek model hai jo (sawaal, chunk) ki jodi ko dono saath padhkar score deta hai. Ise aap sirf ek chhoti list par lagate hain.',
  'Think of writing "from Chapter 3 of the leave policy" at the top of every index card. Contextual retrieval means that before embedding each chunk, you add a sentence, written by a model, that says where the chunk comes from. This fixes orphan chunks, the ones that make no sense on their own.':
    'Sochiye har index card ke upar likhna "chhutti niti ke chapter 3 se". Contextual retrieval ka matlab hai ki har chunk ko embed karne se pehle, aap ek vaakya jodte hain, jo model ne likha ho, jo batata hai ki chunk kahan se aaya. Yeh anaath chunks theek karta hai, jo akele mein samajh nahi aate.',
  'Think of turning a half-spoken "and the second one?" into a full question you can look up. Query rewriting means turning a half-sentence from a conversation into a complete question that can be searched on its own.':
    'Sochiye adhoore bole "aur doosra wala?" ko poora sawaal banana jo dhoondha ja sake. Query rewriting ka matlab hai baatcheet ke adhoore vaakya ko poora sawaal banana jise akele mein search kiya ja sake.',
  'Think of taking out the wrong drawer of files before you start looking. A metadata filter drops chunks that are out of scope, such as the wrong version, date or department, before any scoring happens.':
    'Sochiye dhoondhna shuru karne se pehle galat darawar ki files hata dena. Metadata filter un chunks ko hata deta hai jo daayre ke bahar hain, jaise galat version, date ya department, kisi bhi scoring se pehle.',
  'Think of a hidden note inside the homework that says "ignore your teacher". Prompt injection means instructions slipped into a model\'s input that change how it behaves.':
    'Sochiye homework ke andar chhupi parchi jis par likha ho "apne teacher ki baat mat suno". Prompt injection ka matlab hai model ke input mein ghusaye gaye nirdesh jo uska vyavhaar badal dete hain.',
  'Think of the hidden note being tucked inside a letter that the model opens by itself. Indirect injection is when the attack comes inside content the system reads, such as a document, email, ticket or page.':
    'Sochiye chhupi parchi ek chitthi ke andar rakhi hai jise model khud kholta hai. Indirect injection tab hota hai jab hamla us content ke andar aata hai jo system padhta hai, jaise document, email, ticket ya page.',
  'Think of a house with money inside, a stranger at the door and an open window: all three together are dangerous. The lethal trifecta is private data, untrusted content and a way to communicate outside, all in one system. Any two of the three are safe.':
    'Sochiye ek ghar jisme paisa andar hai, darwaaze par ajnabi hai aur khidki khuli hai: teeno saath khatarnaak hain. Lethal trifecta hai private data, untrusted content aur bahar baat karne ka tareeka, teeno ek hi system mein. Inme se koi bhi do hon toh safe hai.',
  'Think of someone sneaking a diary out of the house through the window. Exfiltration means getting private data out, for example through an email, a webhook, a URL parameter or a rendered image.':
    'Sochiye koi diary ko khidki se chupke se bahar le ja raha hai. Exfiltration ka matlab hai private data ko bahar nikaalna, jaise email, webhook, URL parameter ya dikhayi gayi image ke zariye.',
  'Think of a guard with the master key who opens a door for a stranger because the stranger sounds official. A confused deputy is a component with special privileges that is tricked into using them for someone who has none.':
    'Sochiye guard jiske paas master key hai aur jo ek ajnabi ke liye darwaaza khol deta hai kyunki woh sarkari lagta hai. Confused deputy woh hissa hai jiske paas khaas adhikar hain aur jise bahka kar unka istemal aise insaan ke liye karaya jaata hai jiske paas koi nahi.',
  'Think of the guest list at a wedding gate: only names on it get in. An allowlist is a closed list of destinations that are allowed. It still protects you after an injection succeeds.':
    'Sochiye shaadi ke gate par mehmaan list: sirf usmein likhe naam andar jaate hain. Allowlist un jagahon ki band list hai jinki ijaazat hai. Injection safal hone ke baad bhi yeh aapko bachati hai.',
  'Think of a second student marking the homework. LLM-as-judge means using a model to grade outputs against a rubric. You check the marker against the teacher first.':
    'Sochiye doosra student jo homework check karta hai. LLM-as-judge ka matlab hai ek model se outputs ko rubric ke saamne grade karwana. Pehle aap us marker ko teacher ke saath milakar parakhte hain.',
  'Think of how often the second student gives the same marks as the teacher. Judge agreement is how often the judge agrees with human labels. This number tells you whether the judge is usable.':
    'Sochiye doosra student kitni baar teacher jaise hi number deta hai. Judge agreement hai ki judge kitni baar insaani labels se sehmat hota hai. Yeh number batata hai ki judge kaam ka hai ya nahi.',
  'Think of reading the wrong answers one by one and sorting them into piles, like sorting complaints. Error analysis is reading real outputs and sorting the failures into named groups as you go. It is the most useful single activity in the field.':
    'Sochiye galat jawaabon ko ek-ek padhkar dheriyon mein baantna, jaise shikaayaton ko baantna. Error analysis asli outputs padhkar failures ko naam wale groups mein baantna hai. Yeh is kshetra ki sabse kaam ki akeli gatividhi hai.',
  'Think of your own labelled piles of complaints, taken from your own shop. A failure taxonomy is your own named categories of failure, taken from your own traffic.':
    'Sochiye shikaayaton ki aapki apni labelled dheriyan, aapki apni dukaan se li hui. Failure taxonomy aapki apni failure ki naam wali categories hain, aapke apne traffic se li hui.',
  'Think of the checklist a pilot runs through before every take-off. A regression suite is the cases that must pass before any release ships.':
    'Sochiye woh checklist jo pilot har udaan se pehle dekhta hai. Regression suite woh cases hain jinhe kisi bhi release ke jaane se pehle paas hona hi hoga.',
  'Think of a mock test before the exam versus the marks you get after. Offline vs online eval: offline means testing against an answer key before release. Online means looking at what users get after release.':
    'Sochiye exam se pehle ka mock test aur baad mein milne wale marks mein farq. Offline vs online eval: offline ka matlab hai release se pehle answer key ke saamne test karna. Online ka matlab hai release ke baad dekhna ki users ko kya milta hai.',
  'Think of paying for every SMS, including the ones you send again. Cost per query is the full cost of one request the user can see, including retries and agent steps.':
    'Sochiye har SMS ka paisa dena, un ka bhi jo aap dobara bhejte hain. Cost per query ek request ki poori laagat hai jo user dekh sakta hai, retries aur agent steps ke saath.',
  'Think of asking the junior clerk first, and sending the file up to the senior only if the junior is unsure. A cascade is trying the cheap model first and moving up to a bigger one if a check fails. It is the main pattern for controlling cost in production.':
    'Sochiye pehle junior clerk se poochhna, aur file senior ke paas tabhi bhejna jab junior ko pakka na ho. Cascade pehle sasta model aazmana hai aur check fail hone par bade model par jaana. Production mein laagat sambhalne ka yeh mukhya tareeka hai.',
  'Think of a post office sorting each letter to the right van. Model routing means choosing a model for each request, based on how hard that request is.':
    'Sochiye dak ghar jo har chitthi ko sahi gaadi mein daalta hai. Model routing ka matlab hai har request ke liye ek model chunna, is hisaab se ki woh request kitni mushkil hai.',
  'Think of a tea stall\'s profit on each single cup. Unit economics is the cost and revenue for each unit of use. This number decides whether a feature survives.':
    'Sochiye chai ki tapri ka har ek cup par munafa. Unit economics use ki har ikai ki laagat aur kamayi hai. Yahi number tay karta hai ki feature bachega ya nahi.',
  'Think of a parrot that can read both pictures and words. A vision-language model reads images and text together.':
    'Sochiye ek tota jo tasveerein aur shabd dono padh sakta hai. Vision-language model images aur text ko saath padhta hai.',
  'Think of keeping a whole page photo as one index card. Page-as-chunk means using a whole rendered page as the unit you retrieve, instead of a span of text.':
    'Sochiye poore page ki photo ko ek index card ki tarah rakhna. Page-as-chunk ka matlab hai poore dikhaye hue page ko retrieve hone wali ikai banana, text ke tukde ke bajaye.',
  'Think of a photocopy that loses the drawings and shows only the words. A modality gap is information that is on the page but missing from the text pulled out of it.':
    'Sochiye photocopy jisme chitra chhoot jaate hain aur sirf shabd dikhte hain. Modality gap woh jaankari hai jo page par hai lekin usse nikaale gaye text mein nahi hai.',
  'Think of knowing when the other person has finished speaking so you can reply. Turn detection means deciding when a speaker has finished talking. It is the core problem of voice interfaces.':
    'Sochiye yeh pehchaanna ki saamne wala bol chuka hai taaki aap jawaab de sakein. Turn detection ka matlab hai tay karna ki bolne wala kab bol chuka. Voice interfaces ki yahi sabse badi samasya hai.',
  'Think of a lift check: a children\'s ride is checked more strictly than a bench. A risk tier is how strict your obligations are. It depends on what happens if the system is wrong, not on the technology.':
    'Sochiye jhoole ki jaanch: bachchon ka jhoola bench se zyaada kadai se jaancha jaata hai. Risk tier hai ki aapke kartavya kitne kade hain. Yeh is par tikta hai ki system galat hua toh kya hoga, technology par nahi.',
  'Think of the label on a medicine box: what it is for, how it was tested, where it may fail, and who checks it. A system card is a short document describing what an AI feature is for, what it was measured at, where it fails, and who checks it.':
    'Sochiye dawai ke dabbe par label: yeh kis liye hai, kaise jaancha gaya, kahan fail ho sakta hai, aur kaun jaanchta hai. System card ek chhota document hai jo batata hai ki AI feature kis liye hai, usmein kya naapa gaya, woh kahan fail hota hai, aur kaun use check karta hai.',
  'Think of the story of a parcel: who sent it, whether you may open it, where it is kept and for how long. Data lineage is where data came from, what right you have to use it, where it is kept, and for how long.':
    'Sochiye parcel ki kahaani: kisne bheja, kya aap use khol sakte hain, kahan rakha hai aur kitni der ke liye. Data lineage hai ki data kahan se aaya, use istemal karne ka aapko kya haq hai, woh kahan rakha hai, aur kitni der ke liye.',
  'Think of a clerk\'s work that the officer signs off or overrules. Human oversight is a defined point where a person can review the output, and has the authority to overrule it.':
    'Sochiye clerk ka kaam jise afsar manzoor karta hai ya palat deta hai. Human oversight ek tay jagah hai jahan koi insaan output dekh sakta hai, aur use palatne ka adhikar rakhta hai.',
  'Think of staff bringing their own unapproved gadgets into the office. Shadow AI is staff using AI tools that nobody approved. This really happens and can be measured. It is not a made-up worry.':
    'Sochiye karmchaari apne bina manzoor kiye gadgets office mein laa rahe hain. Shadow AI hai staff ka aise AI tools istemal karna jinhe kisi ne manzoor nahi kiya. Yeh sach mein hota hai aur naapa ja sakta hai. Yeh koi kalpanik chinta nahi hai.',
  'Think of a recipe card whose pass mark is a score on a named set of test questions. An AI PRD is a product specification where the acceptance criteria are eval thresholds, measured on a named dataset.':
    'Sochiye recipe card jiska pass mark ek naam wale test sawaalon ke set par ek score hai. AI PRD ek product specification hai jahan acceptance criteria eval thresholds hote hain, jo ek naam wale dataset par naape jaate hain.',
  'Think of ordering the same brand and batch of flour every time, so the rotis come out the same. Model pinning is fixing an exact model version, so the behaviour does not change underneath you.':
    'Sochiye har baar wahi brand aur batch ka aata mangwana, taaki rotiyan ek jaisi banein. Model pinning ek pakka model version tay karna hai, taaki aapke neeche se vyavhaar na badal jaye.',
  'Think of your regular supplier closing down, so you have to test a new one all over again. A deprecation migration is the re-evaluation you have to do when a provider retires the model you use.':
    'Sochiye aapka pakka supplier band ho gaya, toh naye ko phir se parakhna padta hai. Deprecation migration woh dobara evaluation hai jo aapko karna padta hai jab provider aapka istemal kiya hua model hata deta hai.',
  'Think of the main switch on the electric board: one flip and the power goes off. A kill switch is a flag you can flip at once to send traffic to the path that does not use AI. It is not a rollback.':
    'Sochiye bijli ke board ka main switch: ek jhatke mein bijli band. Kill switch ek flag hai jise aap turant palat kar traffic us raaste par bhej sakte hain jo AI istemal nahi karta. Yeh rollback nahi hai.',
  'Think of a shop counter with buttons that you press. An app is a program someone uses, the thing with buttons. It is the app that talks to the model. The model itself has no interface, no memory and no idea that a person exists.':
    'Sochiye dukaan ka counter jisme buttons dabane hote hain. App ek program hai jise koi istemal karta hai, jisme buttons hote hain. Model se baat app karta hai. Model ke paas khud koi interface, koi memory nahi hoti, aur use pata nahi ki koi insaan hai.',
  'Think of the window at a ticket counter: you pass a note through, and a reply comes back. An API is a way for one program to ask another program to do something, over the internet. You never see it. When this book says your app "calls the API", it means your app sent a message to the model provider\'s computers and waited for a reply.':
    'Sochiye ticket counter ki khidki: aap parchi andar dete hain, aur jawaab wapas aata hai. API ek program ka doosre program se internet par kuchh karwane ka tareeka hai. Aap ise dekhte nahi. Jab yeh book kehti hai ki aapka app "API ko call karta hai", matlab aapke app ne model provider ke computers ko ek message bheja aur reply ka intezaar kiya.',
  'Think of a form written as labels and values inside curly brackets. JSON is a plain-text way of writing structured information so a program can read it, like {"role": "user", "content": "hello"}. It is a data format, not code or a database. API requests and responses are written in it.':
    'Sochiye ek form jo labels aur values ke roop mein curly brackets ke andar likha ho. JSON structured jaankari ko saade text mein likhne ka tareeka hai jise program padh sake, jaise {"role": "user", "content": "hello"}. Yeh ek data format hai, code ya database nahi. API requests aur responses isi mein likhe jaate hain.',
  'Think of the exact counter number at a post office where one kind of job is done. An endpoint is the specific web address a program sends its request to. Different endpoints do different jobs: one for chat, one for embeddings.':
    'Sochiye dak ghar ka woh khaas counter number jahan ek tarah ka kaam hota hai. Endpoint woh khaas web address hai jis par program apni request bhejta hai. Alag endpoints alag kaam karte hain: ek chat ke liye, ek embeddings ke liye.',
  'Think of a letter inside an envelope: the payload is the letter, not the envelope. A payload is whatever is inside the request or reply.':
    'Sochiye lifaafe ke andar ki chitthi: payload chitthi hai, lifaafa nahi. Payload woh hai jo request ya reply ke andar hota hai.',
  'Think of a dial on a machine that you set before pressing start. A parameter is a setting you pass with a request, such as temperature, maximum length or which model. The same word also means the billions of internal numbers a model was trained with. In this book it means the setting unless it says otherwise.':
    'Sochiye machine ka dial jo aap start dabane se pehle set karte hain. Parameter ek setting hai jo aap request ke saath dete hain, jaise temperature, maximum length ya kaun sa model. Yahi shabd model ke training se bane arabon andar ke numbers ko bhi kehte hain. Is book mein jab tak alag na likha ho, iska matlab setting hai.',
  'Think of a rough-work page in a web browser where you can type a few lines of code, press a button, and see what happens. A notebook is the tool this book uses so you never have to install anything. Nothing you do in one can break anything.':
    'Sochiye browser mein kachche kaam ka ek page jahan aap code ki kuchh lines likhkar button dabate hain aur dekhte hain ki kya hota hai. Notebook woh tool hai jo yeh book istemal karti hai taaki aapko kuchh install na karna pade. Usmein aap kuchh bhi karein, kuchh toot nahi sakta.',
  'Think of a borrowed kitchen where your code gets cooked. The runtime is the machine actually running your code. In this app it is Python inside your browser tab, so a reload starts a fresh one, and Restore puts your definitions back. A hosted notebook such as Colab lends you a machine for a few hours and then takes it back.':
    'Sochiye udhaar ki rasoi jahan aapka code pakta hai. Runtime woh machine hai jo asal mein aapka code chala rahi hai. Is app mein yeh aapke browser tab ke andar Python hai, isliye reload se nayi shuru hoti hai, aur Restore aapki definitions wapas rakh deta hai. Colab jaisa hosted notebook aapko kuchh ghante ke liye machine udhaar deta hai, phir wapas le leta hai.',
  'Think of opening the shop shutter so that customers can come in. To deploy is to put a change where real users can reach it. Until something is deployed it exists only on your machine.':
    'Sochiye dukaan ka shutter khol dena taaki customers aa sakein. Deploy ka matlab hai badlaav ko aisi jagah rakhna jahan asli users pahunch sakein. Jab tak kuchh deploy nahi hota, woh sirf aapki machine par hota hai.',
  'Think of putting the old signboard back after a bad new one went up. A rollback is putting the previous version back after a bad deploy. It undoes your code. It does not undo a model\'s behaviour, which is why Chapter 18 insists a kill switch is a different thing.':
    'Sochiye naya kharab board lagne ke baad purana board wapas lagana. Rollback bure deploy ke baad pichhla version wapas rakhna hai. Yeh aapka code palat deta hai. Yeh model ka vyavhaar nahi palat sakta, isliye Chapter 18 kehta hai ki kill switch alag cheez hai.',
  'Think of the whole bookshelf your system is allowed to answer from. A corpus is all the documents your system is allowed to answer from, taken together: your set of source material. The plural is corpora.':
    'Sochiye poori kitaabon ki almari jisse aapka system jawaab de sakta hai. Corpus un sabhi documents ka samooh hai jinse aapka system jawaab de sakta hai: aapka source material ka set. Bahuvachan hai corpora.',
  'Think of the index at the back of a book, so you can find a page fast. An index is a prepared copy of your corpus, arranged so searching it is fast. Building one is called indexing. Nothing can be retrieved until it has been indexed.':
    'Sochiye kitaab ke peechhe ki anukramanika, jisse aap page tezi se dhoondh sakein. Index aapke corpus ki taiyaar ki hui copy hai, aise saji ki usmein search tez ho. Ise banane ko indexing kehte hain. Jab tak index nahi bana, kuchh retrieve nahi ho sakta.',
  'Think of an assembly line where each worker\'s output goes to the next. A pipeline is a sequence of steps where each one\'s output is the next one\'s input. Documents go in at one end, an answer comes out at the other. Chapter 7 draws yours.':
    'Sochiye assembly line jahan har kaarigar ka kaam agle ko jaata hai. Pipeline steps ka ek kram hai jahan har step ka output agle ka input hai. Ek sire par documents andar jaate hain, doosre sire se jawaab nikalta hai. Chapter 7 aapki pipeline banata hai.',
  'Think of waiting for your chai after you order. Latency is how long the user waits. It is measured in seconds, and it is a product decision rather than a technical detail.':
    'Sochiye chai ka order dene ke baad intezaar. Latency woh hai jitna user ko intezaar karna padta hai. Ise seconds mein naapa jaata hai, aur yeh ek product decision hai, koi technical baat nahi.',
  'Think of 100 people queuing for chai: p95 is the wait that 95 of them get or better. It describes the slowest fifth of your users, not the typical one. Averages hide these people; p95 is what you design for.':
    'Sochiye chai ke liye 100 log line mein: p95 woh intezaar hai jo 95 logon ko milta hai ya usse behtar. Yeh aapke sabse dheemi paanchve hisse ke users ki baat karta hai, aam user ki nahi. Average in logon ko chhupa deta hai; design p95 par hota hai.',
  'Think of a courier\'s written promise, with a refund if the parcel is late. An SLA (service-level agreement) is a supplier\'s written promise about uptime or speed, with a consequence attached if they break it. A promise without a consequence is a marketing claim, not an SLA.':
    'Sochiye courier ka likha vaada, parcel late hua toh paise wapas. SLA (service-level agreement) supplier ka likha vaada hai uptime ya speed ke baare mein, tootne par nateeje ke saath. Bina nateeje wala vaada marketing ka daava hai, SLA nahi.',
  'Think of a calculator: same sum, same answer, every time. Deterministic means same input, same output, every time. Ordinary software is deterministic. A language model is not, which is the source of most of the surprise in this field.':
    'Sochiye calculator: ek jaisa hisaab, ek jaisa jawaab, har baar. Deterministic ka matlab hai ek jaisa input, ek jaisa output, har baar. Aam software deterministic hota hai. Language model nahi hota, aur isi se is kshetra ke zyaadatar jhatke aate hain.',
  'Think of a conductor making sure each player in the band comes in at the right time. Orchestration means coordinating several steps or several models so they run in the right order and hand results to each other.':
    'Sochiye conductor jo dekhta hai ki band ka har sadasya sahi samay par aaye. Orchestration ka matlab hai kai steps ya kai models ko aise sanyojit karna ki woh sahi kram mein chalein aur ek-doosre ko results dein.',
  'Think of sorting complaints into labelled piles. A taxonomy is a named set of categories. In Chapter 14 it means your list of the ways your system fails, in your own words, with a count against each.':
    'Sochiye shikaayaton ko labelled dheriyon mein baantna. Taxonomy categories ka ek naam wala set hai. Chapter 14 mein iska matlab hai aapki woh list ki aapka system kaise fail hota hai, aapke apne shabdon mein, har ek ke saamne ginti ke saath.',
  'Think of the note you hand the model: what you want, and how. A prompt is the text your app sends to the model: the user\'s question plus any standing instructions attached to it. It is mostly ordinary English, not a magic phrase.':
    'Sochiye woh parchi jo aap model ko dete hain: aap kya chahte hain, aur kaise. Prompt woh text hai jo aapka app model ko bhejta hai: user ka sawaal aur saath jude tay nirdesh. Yeh zyaadatar aam English hai, koi jaadui vaakya nahi.',
  'Think of the house number on the meaning map, written as a row of numbers. A vector is a list of numbers. When this course says a piece of text has a "position" on the meaning map, the position is a vector: a few hundred numbers describing where it sits. You never look at them.':
    'Sochiye matlab ke naqshe par ghar ka number, numbers ki ek line ke roop mein. Vector numbers ki ek list hai. Jab yeh course kehta hai ki text ki matlab ke naqshe par "jagah" hai, toh woh jagah ek vector hai: kuchh sau numbers jo batate hain ki woh kahan baitha hai. Aap unhe kabhi nahi dekhte.',
  'Think of coaching the model on many examples so it picks up a habit. Fine-tuning is continuing a model\'s training on your own examples so it adopts a behaviour. It teaches shape and register, not durable facts. Chapter 19 is the decision.':
    'Sochiye model ko bahut saare examples se coaching dena taaki use ek aadat pad jaye. Fine-tuning model ki training ko aapke apne examples par aage badhana hai taaki woh ek vyavhaar apna le. Yeh dhang aur lehja sikhata hai, tikaau tathya nahi. Chapter 19 mein iska faisla hai.',
  'Think of the marking scheme a teacher writes before checking papers, so two teachers give the same marks. A rubric is a scoring guide written in advance: what each level of quality looks like, so two people grading the same thing agree.':
    'Sochiye marking scheme jo teacher copiyan check karne se pehle likhta hai, taaki do teacher ek jaise number dein. Rubric pehle se likhi hui scoring guide hai: gunvatta ke har star ka kya matlab hai, taaki ek hi cheez grade karne wale do log sehmat hon.',
  'Think of a clock that slowly runs fast even though nobody touched it. Drift is when behaviour changes over time without anyone changing the code: a model updated, a corpus grown, traffic shifted.':
    'Sochiye ghadi jo dheere-dheere tez chalne lagti hai jabki kisi ne use chhua nahi. Drift tab hai jab vyavhaar samay ke saath badal jaata hai bina kisi ke code badle: model update hua, corpus badha, traffic badla.',
  'Think of a shop\'s ledger that lets someone check later what happened and why. An audit trail is a record of what the system did and why, kept so someone can check it afterwards.':
    'Sochiye dukaan ka bahi-khata jisse baad mein koi dekh sake ki kya hua aur kyun. Audit trail system ne kya kiya aur kyun, uska record hai, taaki koi baad mein jaanch sake.',
  'Think of asking "which of these two mangoes is sweeter?" instead of rating one out of ten. Pairwise comparison is asking which of two answers is better, instead of scoring one answer out of ten. It is more reliable, because people and models are better at comparing than at grading.':
    'Sochiye poochhna "in do aamon mein kaun sa meetha hai?" na ki ek aam ko dus mein se number dena. Pairwise comparison yeh poochhna hai ki do jawaabon mein se kaun sa behtar hai, ek jawaab ko dus mein se score karne ke bajaye. Yeh zyaada bharosemand hai, kyunki log aur models grade karne se behtar tulna karte hain.',
  'Think of a teacher who gives higher marks to the longer essay, even if it says nothing extra. Verbosity bias is a grader\'s habit of scoring longer answers higher, even when they say nothing extra.':
    'Sochiye teacher jo lambe nibandh ko zyaada number deta hai, chahe usmein kuchh naya na ho. Verbosity bias grader ki woh aadat hai ki lambe jawaabon ko zyaada score de, chahe woh kuchh extra na kahein.',
  'Think of a judge who likes whichever dish was tasted first. Position bias is a grader\'s habit of preferring whichever answer it was shown first.':
    'Sochiye judge jise woh dish pasand aati hai jo pehle chakhi gayi. Position bias grader ki woh aadat hai ki jo jawaab use pehle dikhaya gaya woh use zyaada pasand aaye.',
  'Think of the average price per cup when some cups are costly tea and some are cheap tea. A blended rate is what you pay per query on average once traffic is spread across several models at different prices.':
    'Sochiye har cup ki average keemat jab kuchh cup mehengi chai ke hon aur kuchh sasti ke. Blended rate woh hai jo aap har query par average mein dete hain jab traffic alag keemat wale kai models mein bant jaata hai.',
  'Think of a shopkeeper charging less because he remembers your usual order. The cache hit rate is the share of your input that the provider recognised from a previous request and charged less for.':
    'Sochiye dukaandaar jo kam paisa leta hai kyunki use aapka roz ka order yaad hai. Cache hit rate aapke input ka woh hissa hai jise provider ne pichhli request se pehchaana aur kam daam liya.',
  'Think of a parrot that can look at a picture as well as read. A vision model reads pictures as well as text, so you can hand it a page image instead of extracted text.':
    'Sochiye tota jo tasveer dekh bhi sakta hai aur padh bhi sakta hai. Vision model tasveerein aur text dono padhta hai, isliye aap use nikaale hue text ke bajaye page ki image de sakte hain.',
  'Think of a typist who copies the words off a photo of a page but ignores how the page looks. OCR is software that turns a picture of a page into text. It keeps the words and throws away the layout.':
    'Sochiye typist jo page ki photo se shabd utaarta hai lekin page kaisa dikhta hai us par dhyaan nahi deta. OCR software hai jo page ki tasveer ko text mein badalta hai. Yeh shabd rakhta hai aur layout phenk deta hai.',
  'Think of where the rows, columns and boxes sit on a form. Layout is where things sit on a page: rows, columns, boxes. It carries meaning that plain text loses.':
    'Sochiye form par rows, columns aur boxes kahan hain. Layout woh hai ki cheezein page par kahan baithi hain: rows, columns, boxes. Ismein woh matlab hota hai jo saada text kho deta hai.',
  'Think of someone cutting in while you are still speaking. Barge-in is a person talking over the system mid-sentence. Voice interfaces have to handle it; text ones never face it.':
    'Sochiye koi aap ke bolte-bolte beech mein bol pade. Barge-in tab hota hai jab koi insaan system ke beech vaakya mein uske upar bol deta hai. Voice interfaces ko ise sambhalna padta hai; text wale ko yeh kabhi nahi jhelna padta.',
  'Think of which country\'s vault your valuables are kept in. Data residency is which country your data is physically stored and processed in.':
    'Sochiye aapka keemti saaman kis desh ki tijori mein rakha hai. Data residency yeh hai ki aapka data kis desh mein asal mein store aur process hota hai.',
  'Think of the shop handing your parcel to a courier you never met. A subprocessor is another company your provider passes your data to. Their risk becomes yours.':
    'Sochiye dukaan aapka parcel ek aise courier ko de deti hai jisse aap kabhi nahi mile. Subprocessor ek aur company hai jise aapka provider aapka data deta hai. Unka risk aapka ban jaata hai.',
  'Think of the pass mark a paper must reach before the result is announced. An eval threshold is the number a release has to hit before it ships. It is an acceptance criterion with a figure in it.':
    'Sochiye woh pass mark jo copy ko result nikalne se pehle chhoona hota hai. Eval threshold woh number hai jise release ko jaane se pehle chhoona hota hai. Yeh ek acceptance criterion hai jisme ek aankda hai.',
  'Think of opening a new shop branch for one lane first, and widening only if it goes well. A staged rollout means releasing to a small slice of users first and watching the numbers before going wider.':
    'Sochiye nayi dukaan pehle ek gali mein kholna, aur sab theek raha tabhi badhana. Staged rollout ka matlab hai pehle users ke ek chhote hisse ko release dena aur numbers dekhna, phir aage badhna.',
  'Think of a student copying the best notes of a topper on one subject. Distillation is training a small model to copy a large one on one narrow job. You get most of the quality at a fraction of the cost.':
    'Sochiye student jo ek vishay ke topper ke sabse achhe notes utaarta hai. Distillation ek chhote model ko bade model ki nakal karna sikhana hai ek sankre kaam par. Aapko zyaadatar quality kuchh hi laagat par mil jaati hai.',
  'Think of luggage that you can carry from one train to another. Portability is whether an improvement survives changing providers. A better prompt and index travel with you; a tuned model does not.':
    'Sochiye saaman jo aap ek train se doosri train mein le ja sakte hain. Portability yeh hai ki kya sudhaar provider badalne par bhi bacha rehta hai. Behtar prompt aur index aapke saath jaate hain; tune kiya hua model nahi jaata.',
  'Think of a doctor naming the illness, with counts from the tests, before giving any medicine. Diagnosis is naming which kind of wrong you have, with counts, before choosing what to change.':
    'Sochiye doctor jo dawai dene se pehle bimaari ka naam batata hai, jaanchon ki ginti ke saath. Diagnosis yeh naam dena hai ki aapke saath kis tarah ki galti hai, ginti ke saath, kuchh badalne se pehle.',
  'Think of a traffic light: green, amber and red each tell the driver what to do. An interface contract is what the product promises to show at each level of certainty, and what it lets the user do about it.':
    'Sochiye traffic light: hara, peela aur laal, har ek driver ko batata hai ki kya karna hai. Interface contract woh hai jo product vaada karta hai ki woh yakeen ke har star par dikhayega, aur user ko uske baare mein kya karne dega.',
  'Think of a footnote that opens at the exact line, not just the name of the book. A resolvable citation is a source link that opens the exact passage the claim came from, not just the name of a document.':
    'Sochiye footnote jo ekdum sahi line par khulta hai, sirf kitaab ka naam nahi. Resolvable citation ek source link hai jo wahi ansh kholta hai jahan se daava aaya, sirf document ka naam nahi.',
  'Think of the "report a mistake" counter in a shop. A correction path is how a user fixes a wrong output, and what that fix records for you.':
    'Sochiye dukaan mein "galti batayein" ka counter. Correction path yeh hai ki user galat output kaise theek karta hai, aur woh sudhaar aapke liye kya record karta hai.',
  'Think of a lift that still works as a staircase when the power goes. Graceful degradation is what the feature can still do when the AI part is switched off.':
    'Sochiye lift jo bijli jaane par bhi seedhi ki tarah kaam aati hai. Graceful degradation yeh hai ki AI wala hissa band hone par bhi feature kya kar sakta hai.',
  'Think of a labelled box that holds one thing. A variable is a name that holds a value, so later lines of code can use it. In city = "Pune", the name city is the variable. Read the equals sign as "is now".':
    'Sochiye label laga dabba jisme ek cheez rakhi ho. Variable ek naam hai jo ek value rakhta hai, taaki code ki aage ki lines use istemal kar sakein. city = "Pune" mein naam city variable hai. Barabar ke nishaan ko "ab hai" padhiye.',
  'Think of a phone book: look up a name, get its value. A dictionary in Python is pairs of a label and a value inside curly braces, like a small form: {"role": "user", "content": "hello"}. Every message to a model is written this way.':
    'Sochiye phone book: naam dekho, value pao. Python mein dictionary label aur value ki jodiyan hain curly braces ke andar, ek chhote form jaisi: {"role": "user", "content": "hello"}. Model ko bheja har message isi tarah likha jaata hai.',
  'Think of showing a new cook two or three finished dishes before asking him to cook. Few-shot means putting two or three worked examples of the task inside the prompt, so the model copies their pattern. Zero-shot means asking with no examples at all.':
    'Sochiye naye rasoiye ko pakane se pehle do-teen bane hue pakwaan dikhana. Few-shot ka matlab hai prompt ke andar kaam ke do ya teen hal kiye examples rakhna, taaki model unka dhancha copy kare. Zero-shot ka matlab hai bina kisi example ke poochhna.',
  'Think of the teacher\'s answer key: questions you know the right answer to. An eval (short for evaluation) is running a system on cases whose right answers you already know, and counting how many it gets right. The cases together are an eval set.':
    'Sochiye teacher ki answer key: sawaal jinke sahi jawaab aap jaante hain. Eval (evaluation ka chhota roop) ek system ko un cases par chalana hai jinke sahi jawaab aap pehle se jaante hain, aur ginna ki kitne sahi aaye. Saare cases milkar eval set kehlate hain.',
  'Think of a form with fixed boxes, described in writing. A JSON schema is a written description of the exact shape a piece of JSON must have: which fields, of what type, and which are required. A program checks each answer against it.':
    'Sochiye fixed khaanon wala form, jiska vivaran likha ho. JSON schema is baat ka likha vivaran hai ki JSON ke ek tukde ka theek kya aakar hona chahiye: kaun se fields, kis type ke, aur kaun se zaroori. Ek program har jawaab ko isse milakar dekhta hai.',
  'Think of someone\'s diary: the law says how you may use it and when you must give it back or destroy it. The DPDP Act is India\'s Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, with its Rules from 2025. It says what an organisation must do before it collects, uses or shares personal data, such as asking for consent.':
    'Sochiye kisi ki diary: kanoon batata hai ki aap use kaise istemal kar sakte hain aur kab wapas dena ya nasht karna hai. DPDP Act India ka Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 hai, jiske Rules 2025 se hain. Yeh batata hai ki koi sansthan personal data jama karne, istemal karne ya share karne se pehle kya kare, jaise sahmati maangna.',
  'Think of the house rules, the notice board and the named elder who answers if something goes wrong. Governance is the rules, documents and named people that decide how an AI system may be used, who checks it, and who answers for it when it goes wrong.':
    'Sochiye ghar ke niyam, notice board aur woh naam wale bade jo kuchh bigadne par jawaab dete hain. Governance woh niyam, documents aur naam wale log hain jo tay karte hain ki AI system ka istemal kaise ho sakta hai, use kaun jaanchta hai, aur bigadne par kaun jawabdeh hai.',
  'Think of how many cups of chai a stall serves in an hour. Throughput is how much work a system gets through in a given time, such as requests per minute. Latency is how long one request waits; throughput is how many get done.':
    'Sochiye ek tapri ghante bhar mein kitne cup chai deti hai. Throughput woh hai ki ek system diye hue samay mein kitna kaam nipta leta hai, jaise requests per minute. Latency ek request ka intezaar hai; throughput yeh hai ki kitne ho gaye.',
  'Think of giving two groups of customers two different menus on the same day, and counting which sells more. An A/B test shows two versions to two random groups of users at the same time and compares one number between them, so you can tell which version caused the difference.':
    'Sochiye do groups ke customers ko ek hi din do alag menu dena, aur ginna ki kaun sa zyaada bikta hai. A/B test do random groups ke users ko ek hi samay par do versions dikhata hai aur dono ke beech ek number ki tulna karta hai, taaki aap bata sakein ki farq kis version ne kiya.',
});
